{"entryType":"UniProtKB reviewed (Swiss-Prot)","primaryAccession":"C5B164","uniProtkbId":"LANM_METEA","entryAudit":{"firstPublicDate":"2024-07-24","lastAnnotationUpdateDate":"2026-01-28","lastSequenceUpdateDate":"2009-07-28","entryVersion":101,"sequenceVersion":1},"annotationScore":5.0,"organism":{"scientificName":"Methylorubrum extorquens (strain ATCC 14718 / DSM 1338 / JCM 2805 / NCIMB 9133 / AM1)","commonName":"Methylobacterium extorquens","taxonId":272630,"lineage":["Bacteria","Pseudomonadati","Pseudomonadota","Alphaproteobacteria","Hyphomicrobiales","Methylobacteriaceae","Methylorubrum"]},"proteinExistence":"1: Evidence at protein level","proteinDescription":{"recommendedName":{"fullName":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000303","source":"PubMed","id":"30351021"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000303","source":"PubMed","id":"30352145"}],"value":"Lanmodulin"},"shortNames":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000303","source":"PubMed","id":"30351021"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000303","source":"PubMed","id":"30352145"}],"value":"LanM"}]},"alternativeNames":[{"fullName":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000303","source":"PubMed","id":"30351021"}],"value":"Lanthanide-binding protein"},"shortNames":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000303","source":"PubMed","id":"30351021"}],"value":"Ln(3+)-binding protein"}]}],"flag":"Precursor"},"genes":[{"geneName":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000303","source":"PubMed","id":"30351021"}],"value":"lanM"},"orderedLocusNames":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000312","source":"EMBL","id":"ACS39628.1"}],"value":"MexAM1_META1p1786"}]}],"comments":[{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"30351021"}],"value":"High-affinity lanthanide (Ln)-binding protein. Shows 100 million-fold selectivity for La(3+) over Ca(2+). Binds 3 equiv of Ln(3+) with picomolar affinity and a fourth with approximately micromolar affinity. May be involved in receiving and then transporting lanthanides (such as La(3+), Nd(3+) and Sm(3+)) to a specific periplasmic destination"}],"commentType":"FUNCTION"},{"commentType":"BIOPHYSICOCHEMICAL PROPERTIES","phDependence":{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"32686425"}],"value":"REE-LanM complexes are remarkably resilient under acidic conditions, retaining REE binding down to pH 2.5."}]},"temperatureDependence":{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"32686425"}],"value":"REE-LanM complexes are stable over a broad temperature range (up to 95 degrees Celsius)."}]}},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"30351021"}],"value":"Monomer"}],"commentType":"SUBUNIT"},{"commentType":"SUBCELLULAR LOCATION","subcellularLocations":[{"location":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000305","source":"PubMed","id":"30351021"}],"value":"Periplasm","id":"SL-0200"}}]},{"commentType":"MASS SPECTROMETRY","method":"MALDI","molWeight":11759.574,"molWeightError":0.0,"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"30351021"}]},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"32686425"}],"value":"Has been used for metal extraction from two distinct rare-earth elements (REEs)-containing industrial feedstocks covering a broad range of REE and non-REE concentrations, namely, precombustion coal (lignite) and electronic waste leachates. After only a single all-aqueous step, quantitative and selective recovery of the REEs from all non-REEs initially present (Li, Na, Mg, Ca, Sr, Al, Si, Mn, Fe, Co, Ni, Cu, Zn, and U) was achieved, demonstrating the universal selectivity of LanM for REEs against non-REEs and its potential application even for industrial low-grade sources"}],"commentType":"BIOTECHNOLOGY"},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000305"}],"value":"Lanthanides are essential cofactors in some pyrroloquinoline quinone (PQQ)-dependent alcohol dehydrogenase enzymes in the methylotrophic bacterium M.e